now the final habit in Covey's seven  Habits of Highly Effective People is  what he called sharpening the saw in  other words doing things too if you're a  manager you want to work on making sure  you have good values he stresses values  in his book you know developing certain  skills whether it be the ability to use  certain modern technology or if you're a  professional in some field you need to  constantly take courses to make sure  you're up-to-date and so forth in the  case of language learning there are a  number of ways in which we can sort of  sharpen our saw one of them is simply  through exposure to the language and  building up your vocabulary because a  good vocabulary is gonna help you in  every situation also I find that an  occasional review of grammar especially  if the grammar is heavy two examples  rather than explanations the brain has  trouble dealing with theoretical  explanations but the brain is very good  at at creating at recognizing patterns  and creating connections that relate to  patterns so I find it useful to review  patterns so that it makes me more  conscious of certain structures and then  I start to notice them better so that an  occasional review of grammar another way  of sharpening the saw is actually to  start speaking because it's all gonna  make you more attentive but but if we  take this this this sort of image of  sharpening the saw so we are doing  something that is not urgent in other  words rather than sort of being all  concerned about this next engagement  with the language and I won't understand  it I won't be able to say what I want to  say it's thinking that I am doing  something that is going to build up my  skills for the future so what I'm doing  is important but it's not urgent I'm  developing my skills therefore I have  this sense of of and we can you know  satisfaction achievement I'm doing  things to improve my skills and the  benefits will come will come later on  and so I think we can have a sort of  sharpening the saw  to all of our language learning  activities so that we don't get  discouraged when we feel that we're not  making as much progress as as we would  like because all of our activities are  actually improving our skills and the  benefits will flow to us later on so  there it is I've tried to in these short  videos kind of go over again how cubbies  seven Habits of Highly Effective People  has application for us in our language  learning and I hope it kind of helps to  stimulate you to put that effort in to  you know reaching your language goals  thank you for listening bye
 

